### How to use it

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <title>x‑details demo</title>
  <!-- Load the component (the script above) -->
  <script type="module" src="x-details.js"></script>
</head>
<body>

  <x-details>
    <!-- Header shown next to the toggle button -->
    <span slot="header">Header here</span>

    <!-- Always visible while the component is collapsed -->
    <div slot="intro">intro part always visible</div>

    <!-- Visible only when expanded -->
    <div slot="details">details part - visible when expanded</div>
  </x-details>

</body>
</html>
```

**What happens**

* **Collapsed (default)**  
  * The header (with a **+** square) and the intro text are displayed.  
  * Below the intro a **“expand more”** button appears.  

* **Expanded (clicking the + button or the “expand more” button)**  
  * The header stays, the **‑** square appears, the intro disappears, and the **details** slot content is revealed.  

All styling (border, larger font, square toggle) lives inside the component’s Shadow DOM, so it won’t leak out or be affected by the page’s CSS.

